<!--
  Chapter 62 — Unit, Slice & Testcontainers Tests.
    coupon/    CouponRedemptions: FIRST20 once per customer, with ON CONFLICT and with the portable check-then-insert
    testing/   PostgresContainer (start, wait, URL, remove, reuse: what Testcontainers' PostgreSQLContainer does) and
               Isolation (rollback, truncate, a database per test from a template)
    test/      PostgresExtension (one container per run in JUnit's root store; a database per test), the coupon rule
               on PostgreSQL, and H2's limits pinned as tests
  verify/run.sh measures container lifecycles, isolation strategies and the H2 gap. With Spring Boot, the same
  patterns are @ServiceConnection containers, @JdbcTest/@DataJpaTest slices and the test context cache.
-->
